ered","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.td_text.sf_city_hall_wedding.9k0l1m2n":"SF City Hall Wedding (guide)","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.td_text.23_vs_169_wedding.1o2p3q4r":"2:3 vs 16:9 wedding guide","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.td_text.no_tool.5s6t7u8v":"No tool","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.td_text.n_a.9w0x1y2z":"n/a","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.td_text.not_offered.3a4b5c6d":"Not offered","tools.crop-wedding-photo-for-reels.p_text.most_crop_tools_require_manu.5m6n7o8p":"Most crop tools require you to manually center the bride and groom for each of 100+ wedding photos. WeddingAI.video’s crop uses an off-center bias instead of face detection: it shifts the crop window 60% down on landscape sources, where wedding couples usually stand, so the couple stays inside the frame instead of being cropped out. It exports 9:16 + 1:1 + 4:5 in one batch. Plus, the same batch feeds into the AI video’s IG-ready export — vertical Reels + horizontal YT Shorts + 1:1 square for feed + 4:5 for IG carousel."}